rchive/2026-10-22.html</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://aboutali.github.io/bxl_eda_worker/archive/2026-10-22.html</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:38:00 +0000</pubDate><description>34 items, 10 Swiss-relevant.</description></item><item><title>EU FP Digest — 2026-10-21 (37 items)</title><link>https://aboutali.github.io/bxl_eda_worker/archive/2026-10-21.html</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://aboutali.github.io/bxl_eda_worker/archive/2026-10-21.html</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:34:00 +0000</pubDate><description>The European Commission criticized the Trump Administration's waiver of sanctions and tariffs on Russia mandated under the Graham Act, as US envoy Witkoff moved from talks with Zelenskyy in Oslo to a meeting with Putin in St. Petersburg, with EU officials assessing that Washington-Kyiv tensions and a floated three-way summit hand Moscow leverage; von der Leyen signaled the EU will retain Russia energy sanctions despite the US diesel deal, a line Bern will weigh as it calibrates alignment. In parallel, the bloc is seeking €70 billion for Ukraine amid uncertain US backing, courting Canada, Britain and Japan to share costs, while declining Kallas's push for a Black Sea naval mission in favor of possible air policing even as the HR/VP condemned Russian strikes threatening regional shipping and food security. Von der Leyen and Costa condemned Libya's parliamentary ratification of the Libya-Türkiye maritime MoU as a breach of international law and third-party sovereign rights—a statement Switzerland may consider co-signing—reviving Eastern Mediterranean disputes. On the Middle East, the EEAS condemned escalating Houthi attacks as the UK deploys fighter jets to defend Saudi Arabia, and the UNIFIL mandate winds down in Lebanon with a new EU mission to support the Lebanese army but not replace peacekeepers. Kallas also presented an Arctic strategy citing drone incursions, GPS jamming and cable sabotage, framing Russian, Chinese and US competition in the EU's northern neighbourhood.</description></item></channel></rss>
